{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Require all new housing developments to be designated fireworks-free",
        "additional_details": "Unexpected fireworks can cause significant distress to horses, livestock, domestic pets, wildlife and people sensitive to sudden loud noises. We believe new developments should be designed with consideration for surrounding communities and animals.\r\n\r\nThis proposal would apply to newly constructed homes, allowing purchasers to understand the restrictions before buying, without retrospectively changing existing homeowners' rights. Grazing land in particular should be protected from fireworks",
        "background": "Introduce legislation requiring all new residential developments in England to be designated fireworks-free zones, with legally enforceable restrictions preventing fireworks within their boundaries. These restrictions should be recorded in property deeds and clearly disclosed to purchasers.",
